<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Busy Day in Burundi, 1976</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;In 1976, Burundi experienced a coup.&amp;nbsp; This scenario assumes that this resulted in the country suffering widespread unrest, with rebel groups gaining control of military equipment.&amp;nbsp; With the danger of civilian deaths increasing, an international coalition led by&amp;nbsp;France and the&amp;nbsp;United Kingdom has positioned itself to take action.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;This particular scenario focuses on the British effort against the rebels controlling a northern town in Burundi.&amp;nbsp; Future scenarios may look at the efforts by France and other nations during this ficitonal conflict.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
